Trial 1956 has a higher learning rate and lower weight decay compared to 1944. Both have two layers but different max_units and dropouts.

Looking at these top trials, they seem to favor moderate batch sizes (not too small, not too large), relatively high learning rates, and a balance between momentum and weight decay. They also tend to use two layers with a decent number of units and moderate dropout rates.

